  "id": "emotive-imagery",
  "term": "emotive imagery",
  "definition": "Emotive imagery is a communication approach that uses vivid, emotionally engaging elements such as personal case descriptions and pictures to shape how people perceive risk. In this context, it is presented as a form of storytelling that may increase willingness to vaccinate.",
